issues.issue:
The hashes are 12-hex prefixes with ellipses, so they are not verifiable full hashes. Several inputs that determine the result are not pinned:
- the W1 and W3 generation configs;
- the delta logs that fix which W1 and W3 deltas are used;
- `qualify_r1qwen32b.jsonl`, from which the fresh manifest is derived;
- `data/aliases.json` and `data/counterfact.jsonl`, which drive lexical scoring;
- rt.analysis, rt.study2 and metrics, through which salience.py reads;
- the two pre-written abstract files, which §7 says are committed but are not part of the freeze.
The registry entry number is also not given.
